`git log --oneline main..phase2-vastai`:

- `2f3fa32` Load URI::QueryParam in Role::HTTP to fix query_param crash (github #1)
- `645f7b6` Generalize the machine-specific vastai binary path in vast-ai-cli skill (k2, card is `done`)

On `main`, `lib/WWW/VastAI/Role/HTTP.pm:54` calls `$uri->query_param($name => $value)` with only `use URI;` loaded. `query_param` lives in `URI::QueryParam`; it was merged into URI itself only in a recent URI release (in the locally installed 5.35 `URI::QueryParam` is documented as a no-op). `cpanfile` requires `URI` without a version, so on an older URI every request that has `params` (offer search, instance listing with filters, ...) dies with `Can't locate object method "query_param" via package "URI::https"`. Locally (URI 5.35) it works, which is why the suite is green here.

The branch carries the one-line fix, `t/query-params.t` (61 lines) and the `Changes` entry. Since then the skills were renamed on `main` (`vast-ai-cli` -> `vastai-cli`, commit `5e9d17b`), so `645f7b6` will conflict or land in a directory that no longer exists -- check whether the path fix is still needed in `.claude/skills/vastai-cli/SKILL.md`.

Done when: `2f3fa32` is on `main` (or `cpanfile` pins the first URI version that ships `query_param` itself and says why), `t/query-params.t` is in the suite, k2's change is re-applied to the renamed skill if still relevant, and the branch is deleted.

